Source: pg-crash
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ruohang Feng <rh@vonng.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), postgresql-all (>= 217~)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/cybertec-postgresql/pg_crash

Package: postgresql-PGVERSION-pg-crash
Architecture: any
Provides: postgresql-pg-crash
Depends: ${postgresql:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Periodically crash your PostgreSQL database
  If your database is too reliable - pg_crash can kill it for you.
  pg_crash is a PostgreSQL preload module that periodically crashes your
  database infrastructure by sending configured signals to database processes.
  It is intended for HA and failover testing.
